  "notes": "Riot Games: League of Legends, Valorant, Vanguard, Riot Client, Chat/Friends, Store/Banners, Wild Rift, TFT, LoR Riot's third-party dependencies are listed as the specific hosts its client talks to, not as the provider's whole zone. \"*.launchdarkly.com\" meant that switching on the Riot policy proxied the feature-flag traffic of every unrelated application on the network through the operator's VPS. Vivox (in-game voice) is deliberately absent: its media plane is UDP and the proxy has no UDP path, so it lives in forcedDirectGroups instead."
